### About

**About section**

```text
The revenue's there. The lads are flat out. So where the hell is the money going?

That's the question I hear from almost every MD I talk to in M&E and HVAC contracting. Turnover is up, the work is coming in, and yet they're taking less home than two years ago and cannot fully explain the gap.

I spent my career inside building services. Project Engineer at Northern M&E, Contracts Manager at Harlow & Pike, then Operations Director leading the HVAC division. Over five years I grew that division from £4.2m to £11.8m - by shifting the model from one-off installs to planned maintenance contracts and getting disciplined about job pricing so margin held through the growth.

I did not do that by reading about it. I did it by getting into the job costs on live schemes, calling problems while there was still time to act, and building a numbers rhythm the whole operation could run on.

That is exactly what I do now, for MDs who are ready to stop finding out at the final account.

This is for you if:

- You run an M&E, HVAC or electrical contracting firm turning over between £2m and £12m
- You are winning work but the profit doesn't match what you expected when you priced the jobs
- You have retention money sitting out there that nobody in the business is chasing on a proper schedule
- You are still the first call for site decisions, and you've tried delegating it more than once

