```

_Do not explain the offer yet. Get them talking about their situation first. One question, then wait._

**They say: What is it exactly?**

```text
In short: I work with MDs of M&E and HVAC firms who are winning good work but taking less home than they expected, and can't properly explain why. I get into the numbers with them weekly - live job costs, retentions, margin by scheme - and build the rhythm that gives them visibility before the final account lands. I spent fifteen years in building services, finishing up as Operations Director at Harlow & Pike, so there's no warm-up period explaining how it works. Can I ask - which of those three things is biting you hardest right now? Margin, retentions, or being the one everyone rings?
```

_Give them a clear picture, then immediately turn it back to them. Do not list features or pricing at this stage._

**They say: How much is it?**

```text
