_Do not send a brochure or a deck unprompted. Get one or two details first so the follow-up is specific. If they insist on something without answering, send the BOSS Scorecard link with a one-line explanation._

### Avoid

- Explaining the full offer before you know what they actually need.
- Sending a brochure, deck or long explainer to someone who has not asked a real question yet.
- Defending the fee before fit is established.
- Treating 'not right now' as a no and moving on without asking one follow-up question.
- Matching their short reply with a long message - it reads as desperate.
- Using coaching language: accountability, transformation, holistic, journey. It loses the room with this buyer.
- Assuming the problem. Ask which of the three it is, do not tell them.
- Following up the same day if they have not replied. Give it at least 24 hours.

