Aye, happy to be straight with you on that. The MDs I work with invest anywhere from £1,950 a month up to more, depending on what they need and how deeply we get into it. What I'd rather do first is spend half an hour understanding what's actually happening on your schemes - where the margin's going, how the retentions are sitting, whether you're still the one Dave's ringing at quarter to seven. Once I've got a proper picture, I can tell you what makes sense for your situation and you can decide if it stacks up. I've got time on Monday or Thursday afternoon - which works better for you?
