Right, so we've talked through where the margin's going on the live schemes, the retention cash nobody's chasing, and the fact that Dave still rings you before eight. That's fixable. The way I work is we go weekly for the first four to six weeks - I get into your job reviews and pricing discussions, we build the numbers rhythm around your actual costs, and we find where the money's going before the next final account tells you. Then it drops to two ninety-minute sessions a month once the rhythm's running. It's £1,950 a month to start, or if you want to commit to six months we can do that for £10,500 and I'll block the time for you now. Which works better for you - monthly to begin with, or straight into six months?
