| I'd need to run it past my partner / the board / my accountant. | That's fair, and I'd want you to. What I'd ask is this: based on what you've told me today, is the problem real and does the approach make sense to you? If the answer's yes, I'm happy to have a conversation with whoever needs to be in the room. What would help them make the decision? |
| I'm not sure I've got time for another thing on top of everything else. | That's the point, honestly. You're not taking on another project. You're getting someone into the numbers alongside you so you're not carrying it alone. The structure comes from me. You show up to the sessions and work it with me. Most of the MDs I work with find the first month frees up time rather than adds to it, because they stop firefighting blind. |
| How do I know this will actually work for my type of business? | Because it came out of this type of business. I grew the HVAC division at Harlow & Pike from £4.2m to £11.8m by fixing the same three problems you've described today: margin bleed, retentions sitting idle, and the MD fielding every call. I'm not applying a generic framework to your operation. I'm building a rhythm around the way contracting actually works, because I've worked inside it. |

