| 3 | The retention from the job you finished eighteen months ago | Retention cash is earned money. Without one person accountable for chasing every holdback on a fixed schedule, some of it gets quietly written off. |
| 4 | Your accountant is six weeks too late | Management accounts after the period ends cannot tell you whether a live scheme is bleeding margin. Visibility has to be weekly and built around jobs that are still running. |
| 5 | Which jobs actually made money last year? | Most MDs cannot answer this question cleanly. Knowing which clients, contract types and scheme sizes actually make margin changes how the next tender goes in. |
| 6 | The variation that never got agreed | Unconfirmed vars are margin sitting in a grey area. A simple process for logging, submitting and chasing every change order stops the FA coming back short for reasons nobody can explain. |
| 7 | What is the business worth if you step out of it? | A business that only runs because the MD is in the middle of it has no sale value and no step-back. Building a rhythm and clear accountability is how that changes. |
